@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-rules`

-- ca-tests-schedule.l4
--
-- The Schedule to the Interpretation Act (Canada): the fifty-one countries it names as the Commonwealth, one assertion each.
-- Pass 1 asserted six of them; this file asserts every row, the count, and the order, taking the names from the lines of the text
-- (lines 447 to 497 of the plain-text rendering) by a script, so that no name is typed by hand.
-- "The Bahamas" and "St. Christopher and Nevis" are written exactly as the text writes them.

§ `Schedule rows: every country the Schedule names, in the order of the text`

-- row 1: line 447
#ASSERT `is a country named in the schedule` "Antigua and Barbuda"
-- row 2: line 448
#ASSERT `is a country named in the schedule` "Australia"
